Z||000003||rockcrawl||01-05-2001||04:02 PM||||I've seen pictures of the IFG system. The shocks are not replacements for the OEM shocks. They are mounted on the front of the lower control arm with a custom mount, and extend forward at about a 45deg angle to a custom mount on the frame. Not a pretty setup. The air compressor is a POS like you'd buy at K-Mart, a better option would be a Cadillac compressor. Contact Dale Van Blockland van_blok@inetport.com <A HREF="http://www.inetport.com/~van_blok/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.inetport.com/~van_blok/</A>  I think it was his website that had the pictures.<P> I searched through autoparts books looking for an air-assisted replacement for the Fiero shocks. I never found anything small enough.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000004||DISenchanted||01-05-2001||04:17 PM||||I've seen a really nice set.  Let me figure out how much they run.<P>DISenchanted||||reg||1
